*** Claude discovered bug: decompose-ac-pairing

set show timing off .
set show advisories off .

*** _.=._ on two assoc comm terms says false where an instance makes them equal.
*** With X = Y = a both sides are e(a), e(a). Expected for the first reduction: the term
*** left as it is (or an equivalent decomposition), never false. Maude gives false.
*** The other two reductions are for contrast: without the repeated argument the term is
*** left as it is, and the ground instance reduces to true.

fmod AC-PAIRING is
  protecting INITIAL-EQUALITY-PREDICATE .
  sort M .
  ops a b : -> M [ctor] .
  op e : M -> M [ctor] .
  op _,_ : M M -> M [ctor assoc comm] .
endfm

red e(X:M), e(X:M) .=. e(a), e(Y:M) .

red e(X:M), e(Z:M) .=. e(a), e(Y:M) .

red e(a), e(a) .=. e(a), e(a) .
